docs {
  # GET /v1/measuring-points/{id}

  A MeasuringPoint is the **stable identifier** across device replacements.
  Devices come and go; the MeasuringPoint persists. Use this endpoint when
  you already have the `measuring_point_id` (e.g. from a prior consumption
  response) and want its metadata plus the currently installed device.

  `active_device` is the current device, or `null` for difference meters
  (`is_difference_meter: true`) and removed devices. The device history
  (one segment per installation window) comes from
  `GET /v1/measuring-points/{id}/readings`.

  ## Default `id`

  `7c8eb987-8018-40e0-8480-ea1527eeee80` = **WE 01 / water_warm**
  (Musterstraße 2-4) — the measuring point with the meter-replacement demo.
  `active_device` is the replacement device installed on 2025-06-12; the
  two device segments show up in its readings for 2025.

  ## Other measuring points (Musterstraße 2-4)

  | Unit | Metric | Scenario | measuring_point_id |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | WE 01 | heat          | interpolated month end (`degree_day_weighted`) | `27baed27-22fb-49e4-bed6-67871a85b386` |
  | WE 01 | water_cold    | single segment, all measured                   | `eba16a32-148b-4486-b728-d5a1e8706f0f` |
  | WE 02 | water_cold    | `calibration_expired` from 2025-07             | `347321c9-6a5d-45e6-80bf-348bb9e98b12` |
  | WE 03 | water_outdoor | garden tap, installed 2025-04-02               | `e8d86ad4-90d0-4c46-8c49-8e69ace031dd` |
  | WE 04 | hca           | installation date unknown (`installed_at: null`) | `2a206e2f-f8e6-4f98-904d-430c8342cc3d` |
  | WE 05 | hca           | data gap, no readings                          | `443ab660-90fa-4e43-8704-3a335e7703b3` |
  | WE 06 | water_warm    | difference meter, `active_device: null`        | `d246ad75-2df4-45bd-8637-1979060d30a9` |
  | WE 07 | electricity   | reserved metric, no device                     | `acc25994-7a04-4b9b-9275-9bbb43f4b527` |
  | —     | heat          | total heat meter, no usage unit                | `b455c523-12ab-4895-8620-e9422ab4b506` |
}
